; Fleet formatting rules — THE source of truth for every adopted repo.
; Sync law: this file is copied byte-identical to .cljfmt.edn in each
; repo. The CI gate (cljfmt check), the editor (Calva / clojure-lsp),
; and the agent write-hook (clojure-mcp-light) all read the repo copy,
; so system-wide rules and edit-local rules are the same file by
; construction. Changes happen HERE, by a fleet-level commit, and are
; then propagated to the repos — a repo-local edit to .cljfmt.edn is
; drift and fails the fleet config-diff check.
; v1 is deliberately the cljfmt defaults plus ns sorting: the Phase 1
; retro earns every non-default entry, recorded here with its reason.
; LANE DEVIATION (cohost-media-example, 2026-11-22, proposed to the
; fleet in RETRO.md): :sort-ns-references? set to false. Sorting
; :require lists changes namespace LOAD ORDER, which is semantics in
; Clojure, not formatting: with sorting on, the format pass reordered
; cohost.pool / cohost.hosts.auto out of first position in 10 files
; and the demo's coordinator never planned a job (control run on
; pristine sources planned all 10). Form-tree diff proof in STATUS.md.
{:remove-surrounding-whitespace? true
 :remove-trailing-whitespace? true
 :remove-consecutive-blank-lines? true
 :insert-missing-whitespace? true
 :sort-ns-references? false
 :align-associative? false
 :indents {}}
